e:article-doi-10.1007_s12666-022-02638-x a schema:ScholarlyArticle ;
    schema:contentUrl "runs/literature/papers/alloy/2026-09-27_6xxx-corrosion-skku/10.1007_s12666-022-02638-x.txt" ;
    schema:identifier "https://doi.org/10.1007/s12666-022-02638-x" ;
    schema:name "Statistical Analysis of Corrosion Current Density and Tensile Strength of Al-6061 Alloy by Ageing and Retrogression Heat Treatments" ;
    al:notReported "chemical composition given only as supplier ranges (0.45-0.90% Mg, 0.20-0.60% Si, 0.10% max Cu, Mn, Zn, Cr, Ti, 0.35 max Fe), no measured single values",
        "heat treatment parameters (ageing/retrogression temperatures and times) are in Table 1 but no corrosion or strength value is printed for any individual condition",
        "icorr and Ecorr of each individual sample (AS1, CS2, FS3, A1S4, C1S5, F1S6, A2S7, C2S8, F2S9) are only in Fig. 1 and Fig. 2 (figures), no numeric table",
        "no pitting potential, polarization resistance (Rct), corrosion rate, corrosion depth or SCC index reported",
        "temper of the heat-treated samples not stated (only T6 baseline named)",
        "tensile and yield strength values are reported elsewhere [6] and not printed in this paper" .

