e:article-doi-10.26776_ijemm.06.01.2021.04 a schema:ScholarlyArticle ;
    schema:contentUrl "runs/literature/papers/alloy/2026-09-27_6xxx-corrosion-skku/10.26776_ijemm.06.01.2021.04.txt" ;
    schema:identifier "https://doi.org/10.26776/ijemm.06.01.2021.04" ;
    schema:name "Effects of Cooling Rate on the Microstructure, Mechanical Properties and Corrosion Resistance of 6xxx Aluminium Alloy" ;
    al:notReported "Cooling rate values in Table 3 (8.2, 19.1, 3.82, 2.76 °C/min) disagree with the text in section 3.1 (45 °C/s, 50 °C/s, 35 °C/min, 28 °C/min)",
        "Hardness (HV1) and impact strength (KJ/m²) values in Table 3 not extracted (not in the requested property set)",
        "No pitting potential, polarization resistance (Rct), corrosion rate, corrosion depth or SCC index reported",
        "No temper notation given; all samples are as-cast",
        "The mould temperature (140 °C, 230 °C) and ice-block cooling are casting cooling conditions, not a separate heat treatment; they are recorded as steps only to distinguish the four conditions",
        "The paper text describes the microstructure as ferrite and pearlite, which is inconsistent with a 6xxx aluminium alloy; the composition in Table 2 is used as printed",
        "YTS and EL not reported for any specimen (only UTS, hardness and impact strength in Table 3)" .

e:article-doi-10.3390_met9020173 a schema:ScholarlyArticle ;
    schema:contentUrl "runs/literature/papers/alloy/2026-09-25_extract-pilot/10.3390_met9020173.txt" ;
    schema:identifier "https://doi.org/10.3390/met9020173" ;
    schema:name "Effect of Artificial Aging, Delayed Aging, and Pre-Aging on Microstructure and Properties of 6082 Aluminum Alloy" ;
    al:notReported "EL of N + A and P + N + A specimens is only shown in Figure 8c (no numeric values in text)",
        "Hardness values (e.g. 132.32 HV, 102.4 HV, 128.86 HV) are not UTS/YTS/EL and are not recorded",
        "N + A and P + N + A: only maxima over a series of natural-ageing delays (30 min to 48 h) are given in text; the delay of the maximum is not stated, so these were dropped at review",
        "The RT delay time (30 min to 48 h) at which the maximum UTS/YS of N + A and P + N + A specimens was reached is not stated in the text",
        "temper removed at review: the paper never writes T6 (or another temper code)" .

