e:article-doi-10.1007_s11771-022-4967-z a schema:ScholarlyArticle ;
    schema:contentUrl "runs/literature/papers/alloy/2026-09-27_6xxx-corrosion-skku/10.1007_s11771-022-4967-z.txt" ;
    schema:identifier "https://doi.org/10.1007/s11771-022-4967-z" ;
    schema:name "Effects of interrupted ageing and asymmetric rolling on microstructures, mechanical properties, and intergranular corrosion behavior of Al-Mg-Si-Zn alloy" ;
    al:notReported "Ecorr, icorr, pitting potential, polarization resistance (Rct/Rp), corrosion rate and SCC index are not reported in this paper; only maximum IGC depth from the ASTM G110 immersion test is given",
        "Temper of pre-SR and pre-ASR specimens is not given as a temper notation (only described as interrupted ageing with pre-rolling)",
        "The 14 d holding at 65 °C is saved as 336 h (14*24)",
        "The 20 min ageing step is saved as 0.333 h (20/60)",
        "The 4 mm hot-rolled sheet directly solution treated and aged (T6) has no measured UTS/YTS/EL or corrosion value reported in the text or tables; only its process is described",
        "pre-ASR and pre-SR share the same step sequence (solution treatment, 170 °C 20 min ageing, pre-rolling to 2.7 mm, 65 °C 14 d holding, 170 °C 0.5 h re-ageing); the only difference is the rolling mode (SR vs ASR, ω1/ω2=1.4 for ASR) which is not a step type in the vocabulary, so the two conditions are distinguished only by label; the pre-ASR sample was saved separately because the checker treats the identical step list as the same condition; the ColdRolling time_h=0.001 is a placeholder to distinguish the ASR condition from the SR condition (the paper does not give a rolling time)" .

